{\pard\keepn\sb800\sa180\fs34\b\cf1 World Environmental Health Day, 26 September\par}
{\pard\sl400\slmult1\sb40\sa220\fs26\b On World Environmental Health Day, 26 September, Maroma set out how it runs its Auroville workshop, pointing to solar power, less plastic in packaging, and the sorting of materials for recycling as work already in place.\par}
{\pard\sl380\slmult1\sb80\sa180 The company presented these steps as current practice, not a later pledge.\par}
{\pard\sl380\slmult1\sb80\sa180 Split and leftover candle wax is reused. Some is poured into special candles. Some is sold at a lower price to the Auroville community.\par}
{\pard\sl380\slmult1\sb80\sa180 Maroma described the aim as reducing waste, reusing what it can, and making careful choices at each stage of production.\par}
