{\pard\keepn\sb800\sa180\fs34\b\cf1 Ganesh Chaturthi\par}
{\pard\sl400\slmult1\sb40\sa220\fs26\b Maroma marked Ganesh Chaturthi, the festival that celebrates the birth of Lord Ganesha, a figure associated with wisdom, prosperity, and the clearing of obstacles.\par}
{\pard\sl380\slmult1\sb80\sa180 Families and communities gather for prayer, offerings, music, and decorated idols.\par}
{\pard\sl380\slmult1\sb80\sa180 The days usually end with the immersion of the idol in water, a sign of creation and renewal.\par}
{\pard\sl380\slmult1\sb80\sa180 Maroma described the festival as a time of hope and new beginnings.\par}
